\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Round-1 inference pipeline of GMM-Router. The frozen backbone maps input $x$ to routing embedding $\mathbf  {z}$ using layers $0$--$\ell ^*$. The router branch (purple) evaluates the $K$ GMM log-densities, adds the uniform log-prior, and converts scores to routing weights $\bm  {\alpha }(x)$. The expert branch (teal) merges the $K$ LoRA adapters as $\Delta W=\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _k\alpha _k B_k A_k$ and generates output $\hat  {y}$.}}{9}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{5}{9}{Round-1 inference pipeline of GMM-Router. The frozen backbone maps input $x$ to routing embedding $\mathbf {z}$ using layers $0$--$\ell ^*$. The router branch (purple) evaluates the $K$ GMM log-densities, adds the uniform log-prior, and converts scores to routing weights $\bm {\alpha }(x)$. The expert branch (teal) merges the $K$ LoRA adapters as $\Delta W=\sum _k\alpha _k B_k A_k$ and generates output $\hat {y}$}{figure.5}{}}
